.claude
.mcp.json
.venv
build/
work/

# Machine paths. Never committed -- kit.toml's committed half says WHERE things
# are, this says where they are ON THIS MACHINE.
kit.local.toml

# Ghidra's project is an instrument's WORKING STATE, not the record. 2.7M
# across 15 files here, and every byte of it is derived from bin/SILKY.EXE plus
# the loader's defaults -- the database was created on 4 Sep 2026 by importing
# that one file, and no human knowledge has been put into it yet. It is also
# locked and mutating while Ghidra is open, so a commit of it is a snapshot of
# a moving file. What Ghidra has told us so far is in kit.toml as text: the
# block list, and first_para read off the memory map.
ghidra/

# codegen.py writes each probe compile here. Derived, and it changes on every
# run -- a .TPU also embeds a timestamp, so it never compares equal.
probes/out/

# The watched-run staging area. Everything in it is copied from bin/ and
# build/, and a DOSBox config is generated because it carries a machine path.
run/

# Scratch. One-off instruments and their outputs: a script that answers a
# question about THIS target once is not part of the method, so it belongs in
# neither src/ nor kit/ -- WORKING.md's closing-an-iteration test. Anything
# here that turns out to matter gets moved into the record as prose.
temp/
